# INT-SOURCE: ../functional/75_store_through_value.my
# INT-ENGINES: tw default nj noopt
#
# INT unit (#107): a store through a value that is not a variable - a
# call's result, a literal, a ternary, a slice - goes into that value, as
# if it were first bound to a fresh variable (the held root: eval.cpp's
# and the codegen's hold_store_base). The functional program runs as a
# coverage unit too, under the engines above, with no second copy
# (INT-SOURCE); it asserts its own results and every engine must print
# the same.
